Z||000004||stsmithgt||06-25-2001||02:20 PM||||My fuel gauge freaked out a short time before I found out my fuel pump was going out on me.  I had the fuel pump replaced and my gauge is back to normal.||||reg||1
Z||000005||JJ-85-2M6||06-25-2001||04:27 PM||||My gas gauge actually shows less gas than I have!! I usually fill it up, but it shows 3/4 tank.  Occasionally it shows full, but drops down as soon as I go anywhere.  (It uses gas anyway, but not that much!!)  My first Fiero stranded me once, because gauge read a little bit high.  This was 3 years from new and 30,000 plus miles.  I guess it is a universal problem. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||RossT||06-25-2001||11:55 PM||||84...  Mine did the same thing, but it would like to jump around from being pegged to showing how much gas is in the tank.  It's in the sening unit in the tank.  Most likely its all varnished up and you will need to take it apart and sand all the connections to remove the varnish.  You can try to put a gas cleaner thru your system first.  It hepled mine somewhat, but I eventually had to drop the tank.  You will need to take the fuel pump off and take the sending unit totally apart to get at all the connections. Just sanding the resistor wire coils may not be enough.  Before putting it back in test it with an OHM meter.  sould read 0-90 ohms full and empty.||||reg||1
